{"id":"h09t3","name":"Passenger Trips from Flight Legs","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>legs</b> has the columns <code>leg_id</code>, <code>passenger_id</code>, <code>origin</code>, <code>dest</code>, <code>dep</code> and <code>arr</code> (timestamps). Each row is one flight taken by a passenger.</p>\n<p>Sort the legs of a passenger by <code>dep</code>. A leg <b>continues the trip</b> of the passenger's previous leg when both conditions hold: it departs from the airport where the previous leg arrived (<code>origin</code> = previous <code>dest</code>), and the layover (its <code>dep</code> minus the previous <code>arr</code>) is between 45 minutes and 6 hours, both included. Otherwise the leg starts a new trip. Trips are numbered 1, 2, 3... per passenger in time order.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per trip with the columns <code>passenger_id</code>, <code>trip_no</code>, <code>route</code> (the airports of the trip joined with <code>&gt;</code>, for example <code>CMN&gt;CDG&gt;JFK</code>), <code>legs</code>, <code>total_hours</code> (from the first departure to the last arrival, rounded to 1 decimal) and <code>longest_layover_min</code> (the longest layover of the trip in minutes, <code>NULL</code> for a trip with one leg), sorted by <code>passenger_id</code>, then <code>trip_no</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>legs</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>leg_id</th><th>passenger_id</th><th>origin</th><th>dest</th><th>dep</th><th>arr</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>CMN</td><td>CDG</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 11:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>CDG</td><td>JFK</td><td>2026-03-02 12:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 20:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>JFK</td><td>CMN</td><td>2026-03-05 19:20:00</td><td>2026-03-06 02:20:00</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>RAK</td><td>MAD</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 10:30:00</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>MAD</td><td>LIS</td><td>2026-03-02 11:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 12:10:00</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>LIS</td><td>RAK</td><td>2026-03-02 12:55:00</td><td>2026-03-02 14:20:00</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>passenger_id</th><th>trip_no</th><th>route</th><th>legs</th><th>total_hours</th><th>longest_layover_min</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>CMN&gt;CDG&gt;JFK</td><td>2</td><td>12.0</td><td>60</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>JFK&gt;CMN</td><td>1</td><td>7.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>RAK&gt;MAD</td><td>1</td><td>1.5</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>MAD&gt;LIS&gt;RAK</td><td>2</td><td>3.3</td><td>45</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>legs</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>passenger_id</code>, <code>trip_no</code>, <code>route</code>, <code>legs</code>, <code>total_hours</code>, <code>longest_layover_min</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["îlots","LAG","intervalles de temps","string_agg ordonné","array_agg"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>legs</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>passenger_id</code>, <code>trip_no</code>, <code>route</code>, <code>legs</code>, <code>total_hours</code>, <code>longest_layover_min</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"legs":{"columns":[["leg_id","INT"],["passenger_id","INT"],["origin","TEXT"],["dest","TEXT"],["dep","TIMESTAMP"],["arr","TIMESTAMP"]],"rows":[[1,1,"CMN","CDG","2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 11:00:00"],[2,1,"CDG","JFK","2026-03-02 12:00:00","2026-03-02 20:00:00"],[3,1,"JFK","CMN","2026-03-05 19:20:00","2026-03-06 02:20:00"],[4,2,"RAK","MAD","2026-03-02 09:00:00","2026-03-02 10:30:00"],[5,2,"MAD","LIS","2026-03-02 11:00:00","2026-03-02 12:10:00"],[6,2,"LIS","RAK","2026-03-02 12:55:00","2026-03-02 14:20:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["passenger_id","trip_no","route","legs","total_hours","longest_layover_min"],"rows":[[1,1,"CMN>CDG>JFK",2,12.0,60],[1,2,"JFK>CMN",1,7.0,null],[2,1,"RAK>MAD",1,1.5,null],[2,2,"MAD>LIS>RAK",2,3.3,45]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"legs":{"columns":[["leg_id","INT"],["passenger_id","INT"],["origin","TEXT"],["dest","TEXT"],["dep","TIMESTAMP"],["arr","TIMESTAMP"]],"rows":[[1,7,"DSS","CMN","2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 11:20:00"],[2,7,"CMN","IST","2026-03-02 17:20:00","2026-03-02 21:20:00"],[3,7,"IST","DXB","2026-03-02 22:05:00","2026-03-03 02:20:00"],[4,7,"DXB","BOM","2026-03-03 08:21:00","2026-03-03 10:40:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["passenger_id","trip_no","route","legs","total_hours","longest_layover_min"],"rows":[[7,1,"DSS>CMN>IST>DXB",3,18.3,360],[7,2,"DXB>BOM",1,2.3,null]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}